<title>UK: Halifax says UK house prices up 1.2% in Dec.</title>
<headline>Halifax says UK house prices up 1.2% in Dec.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Britain's Halifax Building Society released the following seasonally adjusted UK house price data -</p>
<p> HOUSE PRICES (index base 1983=100)     Dec     Nov     Dec,95</p>
<p> Seasonally adjusted index		 216.3   213.8    199.5</p>
<p> Monthly change (in percent)		 1.2     0.6     0.2</p>
<p> Annual change (in percent)		  8.4     7.2    -1.4</p>
<p>NOTE - The Halifax said the annual rise in house prices was larger than expected in 1996 but the small rise in mortgage rates and prospects of further rises should prevent the market from overheating.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7715</p>
</text>
